---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { EDUCATOR_ON_SALE } from "../lib/plan";

/**
 * An honest comparison with Sight Reading Factory. Their prices are quoted
 * from their public pricing page and dated; recheck before changing them.
 */
const checked = "September 2026";
const rows = [
  ["Who it's for", "Choirs and singers only", "Instrumentalists, bands, orchestras and singers"],
  ["Choral exercises", "Two, three and four parts: SATB, SAB, SSA, TTB and more", "Full ensemble sight reading"],
  ["UIL levels", "Levels 1-5 built in, from UIL's choir criteria", "Customisable settings"],
  ["One teacher or singer", "$19.99 a year (Pro)", "$45 a year (individual)"],
  ["Students", EDUCATOR_ON_SALE ? "100 included with Educator ($99 a year); more at $1 each" : "Educator plan coming soon: 100 included for $99 a year", "From about $3 per student a year"],
  ["Recording and grading student sight-reading", "Not yet. Practice time and exercise counts per student", "Yes"],
];
---

<Layout
  title="A Sight Reading Factory Alternative for Choirs | abc Sight Reading"
  description="abc Sight Reading is a choir-only alternative to Sight Reading Factory: SATB/SSA/TTB exercises, UIL levels 1-5, solfège, and 100 student accounts for $99 a year."
  themable
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-2 text-sr-ink-2 flex flex-col gap-4 pb-10">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-sr-ink">A Sight Reading Factory alternative, made for choirs</h1>
    <p class="text-lg">
      Sight Reading Factory is a good tool that covers every instrument. abc Sight Reading does one thing: sight-reading
      for singers. That focus is why it can write real four-part voice leading, follow the UIL levels exactly, and cost
      less for a whole choir.
    </p>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead><tr class="text-left text-sr-muted"><th class="py-2 pr-3"></th><th class="pr-3">abc Sight Reading</th><th>Sight Reading Factory</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {rows.map(([what, ours, theirs]) => (
            <tr class="border-t border-sr-hairline align-top">
              <th class="py-2 pr-3 text-left font-medium text-sr-ink">{what}</th>
              <td class="py-2 pr-3">{ours}</td>
              <td class="py-2">{theirs}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-sr-muted">
      Sight Reading Factory prices from their public pricing page, {checked}. Sight Reading Factory is a trademark of
      its owner; abc Sight Reading is not affiliated with it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-sr-ink mt-4">When Sight Reading Factory is the better choice</h2>
    <p>
      If you teach band or orchestra as well as choir, want one subscription for all of them, or need students to record
      their sight-reading for a grade today, Sight Reading Factory does that and abc Sight Reading does not.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-sr-ink mt-4">When abc Sight Reading is</h2>
    <p>
      If you teach choir, want exercises that sound like choral writing, prepare for UIL, and want every student to have
      an account without paying per student, try it. Ten exercises a month need no account, a free account gives fifty,
      and solfège (movable or fixed do) and Kodály rhythm syllables are built in.
    </p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a class="sr-btn" href="/choral-sightreading">Try it free</a>
      <a class="sr-btn-quiet" href="/pricing">See pricing</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
